Quick Decision Guide
Need real-time bidirectional? → WebSocket
Need server push only?        → SSE
Need fast service-to-service? → gRPC
Need public API?              → REST
Need flexible queries?        → GraphQL
Need async decoupled?         → Kafka/Message Queue
Need event notifications?     → Webhook
Need IoT/low bandwidth?       → MQTT
Need peer-to-peer video?      → WebRTC

Summary Table
Protocol/Pattern     Direction             Sync/Async         Best For
HTTP/REST         Request-Response            Sync           Public APIs
GraphQL           Request-Response            Sync           Flexible queries
gRPC              Request-Response/Stream     Both           Internal services
WebSocket         Bidirectional               Async          Real-time apps
SSE               Server→Client               Async          Live feeds
Kafka/MQ          Producer→Consumer           Async          Event-driven
Webhook           Server→Client               Async          Event notifications
Long Polling      Request-Response         Sync(fake async)  Simple notifications
WebRTC            Peer-to-Peer                Async          Video/audio calls
MQTT              Pub-Sub                     Async          IoT devices

Transport protocols (TCP/UDP/TLS) are the foundation. Application protocols (HTTP/WebSocket/gRPC) build on top. Communication patterns (REST/GraphQL/events) define HOW you structure the conversation. Pick based on: real-time needs, direction of data flow, internal vs external, and latency requirements. ✅
